.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH tapectl-volume-compact 1  "tapectl-volume-compact " 
.SH NAME
tapectl\-volume\-compact \- Interactive compaction: read + write + finish in one flow
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBtapectl volume compact\fR [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-\-to\fR] [\fB\-\-device\fR] [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR] [\fB\-\-allow\-missing\-escrow\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR] [\fB\-\-prewrite\-hash\fR] [\fB\-q\fR|\fB\-\-quiet\fR] [\fB\-\-fill\-ceiling\fR] [\fB\-y\fR|\fB\-\-yes\fR] [\fB\-\-config\fR] [\fB\-\-full\-confirm\fR] [\fB\-\-force\fR] [\fB\-\-home\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fILABEL\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Interactive compaction: read + write + finish in one flow
.PP
One drive (`\-\-device`) serves both the read and the write, so the flow PAUSES after step 1 for you to unload the source and load the destination — always, with or without `\-\-to`. It therefore needs a terminal, and without one it refuses before reading anything. To compact unattended, run the steps separately: `volume compact\-read <SOURCE>`, swap cartridges, `volume compact\-write \-\-destination <DEST>`, then `volume compact\-finish <SOURCE>`.
.PP
Step 3 applies `compact\-finish`\*(Aqs ADR\-0008 Tier\-2 gate and may refuse non\-interactively without `\-\-force`. When it does, the destination tape is already written and sealed and nothing is lost: `volume compact\-finish <SOURCE> \-\-force` completes the flow without re\-reading or re\-writing anything.
.PP
Exit status: `volume write`\*(Aqs, for step 2\*(Aqs write (0 sealed and confirmed, 2 nothing written, 3 confirm inconclusive, 4 interrupted, 5 aborted, 6 quarantined, 75 catalog busy). A step 1 failure exits 2: step 1 writes nothing. A step 3 failure exits 0 with a warning naming `volume compact\-finish`: the destination is sealed and confirmed and counts as a copy.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Output in JSON format
.TP
\fB\-\-to\fR \fI<TO>\fR
Destination volume label (already initialised). With it, the pause after step 1 only asks you to swap cartridges and press Enter; without it, that pause also asks for the label. It never skips the swap: the destination is written through the same drive the source was read from
.TP
\fB\-\-device\fR \fI<DEVICE>\fR
Tape device (by\-id path). Defaults to the only configured drive; required when more than one is configured
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Show what would be done without making changes. Commands that cannot preview refuse the flag rather than ignore it
.TP
\fB\-\-allow\-missing\-escrow\fR
See `volume write \-\-allow\-missing\-escrow`
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Enable verbose output
.TP
\fB\-\-prewrite\-hash\fR
See `volume write \-\-prewrite\-hash` (step 2\*(Aqs write)
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
No live progress on stderr. Long operations (stage create, volume write/resume/verify/read\-slices, restore) still write their session log under <home>/logs/
.TP
\fB\-\-fill\-ceiling\fR \fI<FILL_CEILING>\fR
See `volume write \-\-fill\-ceiling` (step 2\*(Aqs write)
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR
Skip ADR\-0008 Tier\-2 confirmation prompts. It never reaches a Tier\-3 refusal — those are facts, not risks to accept
.TP
\fB\-\-config\fR \fI<CONFIG>\fR
Path to config file.

NOTE: on its own this ALSO relocates the whole tapectl home to the config file\*(Aqs parent directory — database, keys, staging, stage reports. That is how every test harness gets an isolated home, so it still works, but it is surprising enough that it now warns. Use \-\-home when you mean "operate on a different archive", and \-\-config only to point at a config file inside that home.
.TP
\fB\-\-full\-confirm\fR
See `volume write \-\-full\-confirm` (step 2\*(Aqs write)
.TP
\fB\-\-force\fR
See `volume compact\-finish \-\-force` — step 3\*(Aqs ADR\-0008 Tier\-2 gate. With this (or the global `\-\-yes`) step 3 asks nothing; the cartridge swap after step 1 still waits for you
.TP
\fB\-\-home\fR \fI<HOME>\fR
tapectl home directory: database, keys, catalogs, stage\-reports, logs.

Defaults to ~/.tapectl. The config file is taken from <home>/config.toml unless \-\-config overrides it. Also settable as TAPECTL_HOME.
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
<\fILABEL\fR>
Source volume label
